---
import Head from "../../components/Head.astro";
import Hero from "../../components/Hero.astro";
import Showcase from "../../components/Showcase.astro";
import Records from "../../components/Records.astro";
import Ending from "../../components/Ending.astro";
import "../../styles/home.css";
import "../../styles/system.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <Head
      title="Dunia"
      description="Dunia is an SDK that sits inside a game engine and turns gameplay into labelled training data for robots and physical AI."
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" /><!-- taste-skill-ignore: mono is only for the hero readouts and the export sheet -->
    <script is:inline>document.documentElement.classList.add("js")</script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <Hero base="/" start="ai" aiHref="#demo" aiNote="Dunia, watch the demo below">
      <h1><span class="ln" style="--i:0"><span style="color:inherit">Gameplay in,</span></span> <span class="ln" style="--i:1"><span>training data out.</span></span></h1>
    </Hero>

    <main>
      <Showcase
        id="demo"
        variant="An SDK for game engines"
        fact="MVP running in our demo game"
        say="The video shows the MVP inside our own demo game: someone plays, and Dunia writes down each step as labelled data."
        href="#pilot"
        action="Become a pilot partner"
      />

      <section class="sys sec" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-h">
        <div class="rows">
          <div class="row">
            <dl class="facts" data-rise>
              <div><dt>Product</dt><dd>SDK for game engines</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Output</dt><dd>State, action, outcome, labelled</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>MVP running in our demo game</dd></div>
              <div><dt>For</dt><dd>Robotics and physical AI teams</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <div>
              <h2 id="why-h" data-rise>Why games</h2>
              <p class="lead" data-rise style="margin-top:28px">A robot learns from three things: what the world looked like, what it did, and what happened next. Collecting that with real robots is slow and expensive, and sometimes the robot breaks. A game engine already tracks all three, so nobody has to label anything by hand.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cols">
          <div data-rise>
            <h3>State</h3>
            <ul><li>What the world looked like</li><li>Positions</li><li>Sensors</li><li>Camera</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div data-rise>
            <h3>Action</h3>
            <ul><li>What the player did</li><li>Steering</li><li>Inputs</li><li>Choices</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div data-rise>
            <h3>Outcome</h3>
            <ul><li>What happened next</li><li>Reward</li><li>Collision</li><li>Success</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="sys sec" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-h" style="padding-top:0">
        <div class="rows">
          <div class="row">
            <p class="word" data-rise>How it works</p>
            <h2 id="how-h" data-rise>Three steps, inside the engine</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <p class="word" data-rise>Hook in</p>
            <p class="lead" data-rise>The SDK hooks into the game engine and records state, inputs and outcomes as the player acts.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <p class="word" data-rise>Snapshot each decision</p>
            <p class="lead" data-rise>It saves a snapshot at each decision, not every frame, so the data is dense and small.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <p class="word" data-rise>Export</p>
            <p class="lead" data-rise>Episodes come out labelled, in the format the team using the data trains on, for example RLDS.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <Records />

      <section class="sys sec field-ai" id="pilot" aria-labelledby="pilot-h">
        <div class="row" style="margin-bottom:72px">
          <p class="word" data-rise>Pilot partners</p>
          <div>
            <h2 id="pilot-h" data-rise>We're looking for pilot partners on both sides</h2>
            <p class="lead" data-rise style="margin-top:20px">The MVP works. The next version gets built with the first teams who use it, so it fits a real problem instead of one we guessed at. We ask for a real problem or a real game, and honest feedback.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="tracks">
            <div data-rise>
              <h3>AI and robotics teams</h3>
              <p>Tell us the task and the format you train on. We build a game scenario for it, record real play with Dunia, and you test the labelled data in your own pipeline.</p>
              <p class="soft">You get data shaped for your problem, and a say in what the SDK does next.</p>
              <a class="act" href="#contact" data-topic="ai"><span>Apply as an AI team</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h13M13 6l6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square"/></svg></a>
            </div>
            <div data-rise>
              <h3>Game studios</h3>
              <p>We put Dunia inside a game people already play, record play as labelled data, and work with you on turning that data into a new source of revenue for the game.</p>
              <p class="soft">You get early access to the SDK, and a say in how it fits your engine.</p>
              <a class="act" href="#contact" data-topic="studio"><span>Apply as a game studio</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h13M13 6l6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square"/></svg></a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Ending />

    <script>
      import "../../scripts/hero.js";
      import "../../scripts/site.js";
      import "../../scripts/records.js";
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
